<section>
    <h2>📌 Principle</h2>
    <p>Transparency</p>
    <h2>❓ What</h2>
    <p>Don't hide things from your users. List known limitations on a page, possibly direct to it before user contacts support. List bugs that can be affecting a lot of users (or even all known bugs), and direct to that list as well. If you make a mistake - be open and humble about it: this builds trust with your users, and trust is a feature that isn't easily replicable by competitors. This doesn't mean that you forget security and privacy good practices and laws like GDPR, though.</p>
    <h2>🪙 Business impact</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Duplicate or unnecessary tickets</li>
        <li>Poor communication lines</li>
        <li>Users' trust</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>❌ Poor implementation</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Increases the load on agents through duplicate tickets.</li>
        <li>Blindsides users and stakeholders about critical issues.</li>
        <li>Deteriorates trust.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>✅ Good implementation</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Reduces the number of duplicate tickets.</li>
        <li>Raises awareness of limitations and ongoing issues.</li>
        <li>Builds trust that you can do the right thing.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>🪢 Alignment</h2>
    <p>Service-Level Management and Public Incident Reporting</p>
    <h2>🖼️ Logo</h2>
    <img crossorigin="anonymous" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="float_left gallery_zoom supops_fact" src="/assets/images/supops/facts/transparency.svg" alt="Transparency icon" width="375" height="602">
    <p>Represented by an ethernet cable, because 8P8C jacks used in those are commonly transparent. Ok, because I couldn't think of any other connection to the logo.</p>
    <h2 class="float_clear">🛠️ Common tools</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Notification systems</li>
        <li>Public lists of known issues</li>
        <li>Public list of limitations</li>
        <li>Newsletters</li>
        <li>Blogs</li>
        <li>Internal inter-team communications</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>📊 Metrics</h2>
    {{ include('supops/metrics/transparency.twig') }}
    <h2>💡 Tips</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Have a clearly defined process to notify both stakeholders and users about critical issues and status updates regarding those, while keeping track of notifications' history (what, when, to whom, etc.).</li>
        <li>Define criteria for assigning respective <em>priority</em> and
            <em>severity</em> to a ticket that is used universally across all organizations (bonus points, if they are made public).
        </li>
        <li>If possible, make your ticketing system public (like
            <a href="https://youtrack.jetbrains.com/" target="_blank">JetBrains</a> did, for example).
        </li>
        <li>If the whole ticketing system can't be made public, have a list of current known bugs and update it regularly (ideally make the bugs from the ticketing system public selectively).</li>
        <li>If a security issue was found and fixed, disclose it, thanking the reporter, if it was someone from outside the company.</li>
        <li>Have blog posts discussing complex features or issues resolved by respective teams.</li>
        <li>Where possible, make the code of the software parts used in your product public.</li>
        <li>Register ideas as tickets or similar items, to which tickets can be linked: this will also help prioritize them.</li>
        <li>Consider beta-test programs with end-users to show what you're doing and why, as well as to build trust.</li>
    </ul>
